// ESM build → dist/esm. This is the tree browser bundlers see.
//
// `src/veil` is deliberately excluded. Veil's pairing crypto is the vendored
// wasm-bindgen glue built for the *nodejs* target: it reads the `.wasm` off disk
// with `require('fs')` and instantiates it at module-evaluation time. That is
// not merely un-tree-shakeable in a browser bundle, it cannot run there at all,
// and instantiating WebAssembly costs the consuming origin a
// `wasm-unsafe-eval` in its CSP. Keeping it out of this tree is what lets the
// root and `./crypto` entries be imported with no WASM anywhere in the graph.
//
// Veil is still shipped — from the CJS tree, under the `./veil` subpath.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "ES2020",
    "outDir": "dist/esm"
  },
  "exclude": ["node_modules", "dist", "**/*.test.ts", "src/veil"]
}
